WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.468
-My next guest is
a talented actress.

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:05.938
And starting tonight you can see
her as Monica Lewinsky

00:00:05.938 --> 00:00:08.507
in "Impeachment:
American Crime Story"

00:00:08.507 --> 00:00:11.411
every Tuesday
at 10:00 p.m. on FX.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.779
Please welcome Beanie Feldstein!

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:16.349
♪ -It's Beanie Feldstein ♪

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.851
♪ As we're about to see ♪

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.586
♪♪

00:00:20.586 --> 00:00:23.122
♪ Monica Lewinsky ♪

00:00:23.122 --> 00:00:24.591
♪ When she ain't working ♪

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:26.926
♪ And she got time to kill ♪

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:32.131
♪♪

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:34.667
-It feel good having a crowd?

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.636
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.636 --> 00:00:37.703
-Wow!

00:00:37.703 --> 00:00:38.771
-There's nothing like
a live audience.

00:00:38.771 --> 00:00:40.239
-This is so crazy.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:42.475
It's wild, right?
-Oh, my God. We're back.

00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:43.743
-We're back.

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.678
I want to talk to you
about so many things.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.513
But first off, I want to
congratulate you.

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:51.350
It just was released that you
are going to be the lead

00:00:51.350 --> 00:00:53.385
of "Funny Girl" on Broadway.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:56.422
And I go, "Yes!"
-Wow!

00:00:56.422 --> 00:00:57.623
-That's perfect.

00:00:57.623 --> 00:00:59.091
This is the first time
it's been on Broadway

00:00:59.091 --> 00:01:02.395
in 50 years or something.
-Since 1964.

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:03.596
-Wow.
-Isn't that insane?

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.164
-And, I mean, Barbra Streisand.

00:01:05.164 --> 00:01:07.499
I mean, just -- I know.

00:01:07.499 --> 00:01:10.403
And I was like they couldn't
think of a better,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.471
more perfect person
than you to cast in it.

00:01:12.471 --> 00:01:14.273
I'm so happy it's you.

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:16.742
And then when I said I want to
talk about it on the show,

00:01:16.742 --> 00:01:20.179
you sent over a photo of you
as a child.

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:21.781
-Yeah.
-Was it Halloween?

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:23.249
-This was my third
birthday party.

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.417
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:27.386
I asked for the theme
to be "Funny Girl,"

00:01:27.386 --> 00:01:29.588
as every 2 1/2-year-old does.

00:01:29.588 --> 00:01:31.324
Not Elmo.
Not "The Little Mermaid."

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.992
Please, "Funny Girl"
to be my theme.

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:35.327
-So this is you as Fanny Brice.

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:37.630
[ Audience aws ]
-Yeah.

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:39.766
-Can you believe that
this is happening?

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.667
-No.
-Can you believe life right now?

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:44.403
-I feel like I should teach
a class in manifesting,

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:46.372
but I don't know what I did.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:48.140
I wouldn't know what to teach.
-Seriously.

00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:51.010
I mean, I just think it's
so full circle and so cool.

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.511
I saw you in "Hello, Dolly!"

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:54.247
By the way,
you were phenomenal in that,

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:55.481
and I think you're going to
rock this one.

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:56.515
-Thank you.

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:58.184
-Did you always do musicals
as a kid?

00:01:58.184 --> 00:02:01.521
-I always did musicals as a kid.
I was obsessed.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:02.888
-What kind of kid were you?

00:02:02.888 --> 00:02:04.724
Were you a rule breaker?

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:05.892
Were you a good kid?

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:09.028
-No. I'm a strict rule follower
now.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:12.565
But when I was a kid, I
don't want to say I was a bully

00:02:12.565 --> 00:02:14.567
because that sounds
really horrific,

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.102
and that's the last thing
I would want to be.

00:02:16.102 --> 00:02:20.039
But I'm the third kid,
and I was, let's say,

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.708
like, over, the young kids.

00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:23.009
Right? I was like, "Come on.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:24.109
I want to be with the adults.

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:25.644
I want to be with
the teenagers."

00:02:25.644 --> 00:02:28.248
I didn't -- I couldn't find
my crowd in preschool.

00:02:28.248 --> 00:02:30.783
So I used to carpool --
-Preschool.

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:33.553
-I used to carpool with
this girl, Katie,

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:34.954
who is lovely and wonderful.

00:02:34.954 --> 00:02:39.825
But when we were kids, she
used to cry every single morning

00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:41.093
that her mom would leave.

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.362
And I couldn't take it
after a while, Jimmy.

00:02:43.362 --> 00:02:45.498
[ Laughter ]
And I went up to her,

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.533
and I grabbed her
like where your tie is.

00:02:47.533 --> 00:02:50.670
And I pulled her to my face,
and I said,

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.474
"Katie, the mommies leave
and the mommies come back.

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:56.843
What part of that
don't you understand?"

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.978
[ Laughter ]
And I threw her to the ground.

00:02:59.978 --> 00:03:02.382
And the teachers called my mom,
and they were like,

00:03:02.382 --> 00:03:05.651
"We shouldn't be laughing,
but it was so funny."

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:08.654
-"Mommies drop you off,
and the mommies pick you up.

00:03:08.654 --> 00:03:11.156
Okay? Happens every day."

00:03:11.156 --> 00:03:14.059
-"How is it not getting in that
she will come back?

00:03:14.059 --> 00:03:16.195
I promise you."
-I love that.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:18.764
-So I was such a little meanie,
but then I grew into a Beanie,

00:03:18.764 --> 00:03:20.833
and it was fine.
It was all good.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.937
-Beanie, I got to talk about you
playing Monica Lewinsky.

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:27.140
"Impeachment:
American Crime Story."

00:03:27.140 --> 00:03:28.541
-Yes.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:29.875
-Everyone is talking about it.

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:31.177
I don't know if you've --

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:33.512
You're on every commercial,
on every channel.

00:03:33.512 --> 00:03:34.681
And it's amazing.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:37.950
I've only seen
the first episode, but, man.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:39.718
You got me
right off the beginning.

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:42.021
I go -- I just feel for you
and I go,

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:46.191
"I lived through that at the
time not having these emotions."

00:03:46.191 --> 00:03:49.562
And I'm watching this girl just
kind of scared and in trouble

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:51.263
and like, "What's going on?"

00:03:51.263 --> 00:03:53.065
And, now, Monica Lewinsky
is actually

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:55.201
producing the show as well.
-Yeah.

00:03:55.201 --> 00:03:57.203
-So you got to meet her
and talk to her?

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:58.437
-I did.

00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:00.506
It's been an incredibly
moving experience, Jimmy.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:04.209
I mean, I was in London
when Ryan Murphy called me.

00:04:04.209 --> 00:04:07.013
And he -- I answered this
American number I don't know.

00:04:07.013 --> 00:04:08.181
And I'm like, "Hello?"
and he's like,

00:04:08.181 --> 00:04:09.315
"Beanie, it's Ryan Murphy."

00:04:09.315 --> 00:04:11.484
And I was like --
My butt fell off, okay?

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.752
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:17.055
And he was like, "Do you want to
play Monica Lewinsky

00:04:17.055 --> 00:04:18.958
in the third installment of
'American Crime Story,'

00:04:18.958 --> 00:04:20.359
and do you want to be
a producer?"

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:23.129
And it was the most
empowering moment.

00:04:23.129 --> 00:04:24.964
It was such a massive deal.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:27.033
And it's her real life.

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:30.136
And so we felt that she should
be a part of telling her story

00:04:30.136 --> 00:04:33.138
because in the '90s,
she was actively silenced by

00:04:33.138 --> 00:04:34.273
the Office of
Independent Counsel

00:04:34.273 --> 00:04:35.641
because of her immunity deal.

00:04:35.641 --> 00:04:38.243
She was not permitted to speak
for herself,

00:04:38.243 --> 00:04:40.012
and she was literally silenced.

00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:43.082
So people think they understand
her story

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:46.151
and the stories of Paula Jones
and Linda Tripp, but they don't.

00:04:46.151 --> 00:04:48.421
And we're hoping to really peel
back the curtain and show you

00:04:48.421 --> 00:04:49.922
what was really happening
at that time.

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.623
-Well, you knocked it
out of the park.

00:04:51.623 --> 00:04:52.792
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:04:52.792 --> 00:04:55.094
Here's Beanie Feldstein
as Monica Lewinsky

00:04:55.094 --> 00:04:57.329
in "Impeachment:
American Crime Story."

00:04:57.329 --> 00:04:58.630
Take a look at this.

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.966
-I have to say,
you're such a knockout.

00:05:00.966 --> 00:05:03.736
I just assumed you'd be dating
some big D.C. player.

00:05:03.736 --> 00:05:05.704
-[ Sighs ]
-What?

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:09.975
-I'm not dating.
-Why not?

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:11.310
-I'm kind of in something.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.346
-And yet you feel lonely?

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.880
-Yes, affirmative.

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:18.551
-Well, that's no good.

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:21.687
Tell me about him.

00:05:21.687 --> 00:05:23.756
-It's, uh...

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.925
It's just he's, um, unavailable.

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.461
-Someone long distance?

00:05:28.461 --> 00:05:32.265
Someone from work?

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:36.736
Someone important?

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:38.838
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:38.838 --> 00:05:40.340
-Beanie Feldstein!

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:42.808
"Impeachment:
American Crime Story"

00:05:42.808 --> 00:05:45.912
airs Tuesdays at 10:00 p.m.
on FX.

